---
import Head from '../../components/Head.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import VoiceTimeline from '../../components/VoiceTimeline.astro';
import '../../styles/global.css';

const voiceSteps = [
  { title: 'User speaks', sub: '0 ms' },
  { title: 'speech recognition' },
  { title: 'partial transcript' },
  { title: 'LLM inference' },
  { title: 'first tokens' },
  { title: 'speech synthesis' },
  { title: 'audio response' },
];
---
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <Head
      title="In voice systems, latency is product quality. — Aakash Patel"
      description="A real-time voice AI system where speech recognition, inference and synthesis overlap asynchronously — because every pause makes the product feel broken."
      path="/work/voice-ai"
    />
  </head>
  <body>
    <a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
    <Header base="/" />

    <main id="main">
      <article>
        <div class="wrap work-hero">
          <p class="kicker"><span class="n">03</span> · Case study · Real-time AI</p>
          <h1>In voice systems, latency is product quality.</h1>
          <p class="work-lede">A conversational voice application: speech recognition, LLM inference, and speech synthesis, orchestrated asynchronously over WebSockets. Built to feel like talking to a person, monitored like infrastructure.</p>
        </div>

        <section class="work-section" aria-label="Context">
          <div class="wrap grid12">
            <div class="work-body">
              <h2>Context</h2>
              <p>Three slow operations in sequence — hear, think, speak — with a human waiting on the other end. Run them one after another and the conversation feels broken. The product only works if the whole pipeline fits inside a latency budget a person finds natural.</p>
            </div>
            <aside class="sidenote">
              <p>In a real-time system, a slow stage is a product defect.</p>
            </aside>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="work-section" aria-label="Architecture">
          <div class="wrap grid12">
            <div style="grid-column: 1 / span 12">
              <h2>Architecture</h2>
              <VoiceTimeline steps={voiceSteps} label="Voice pipeline — stages overlap instead of waiting" />
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="work-section" aria-label="Decision and result">
          <div class="wrap grid12">
            <div class="work-body">
              <h2>Decision</h2>
              <p>The pipeline runs asynchronously over WebSockets: recognition, inference, and synthesis overlap instead of waiting on each other. Each stage is monitored like infrastructure — in a real-time system, a slow stage is a product defect.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="work-body" style="grid-column: 8 / span 5">
              <h2>Constraint</h2>
              <p>No stage could be allowed to stall the conversation, and no latency figure could be assumed — the design had to overlap work and monitor every stage, without inventing targets that didn't exist.</p>
              <h2 style="margin-top: 2.5rem">Result</h2>
              <p>A voice system that holds a natural conversation, with latency treated as a feature of the product rather than a number on a dashboard.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="work-section" aria-label="Pull quote">
          <div class="wrap grid12">
            <blockquote class="pullquote">Run them one after another and the conversation feels broken.</blockquote>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="work-section" aria-label="Lessons">
          <div class="wrap grid12">
            <div style="grid-column: 1 / span 7">
              <h2>Lessons</h2>
              <ol class="lessons">
                <li>In voice, every unnecessary pause makes the product feel broken.</li>
                <li>Async overlap is a design decision, not an optimization.</li>
                <li>Monitor real-time stages like infrastructure, because they are.</li>
              </ol>
              <h2 style="margin-top: 2.5rem">Stack</h2>
              <p class="stack-line">Deepgram · Groq · ElevenLabs · Twilio · FastAPI</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <div class="wrap">
          <nav class="work-nav" aria-label="More case studies">
            <a class="tlink" href="/work/enterprise-ai"><span class="arr" aria-hidden="true">←</span>&nbsp;Previous: Production AI</a>
            <a class="tlink" href="/"><span class="arr" aria-hidden="true">←</span>&nbsp;All work</a>
          </nav>
        </div>
      </article>
    </main>

    <Footer />
  </body>
</html>
